<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Angul district</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Angul is a district of central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/odisha">Odisha</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, with its headquarters at the town of Angul. Formed in 1993 from part of Dhenkanal district, it includes the former <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/princely-state">princely states</a> of Talcher, Pal Lahara and Athmallik and the British-ruled area of Angul. Rich in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/coal">coal</a>, it is a centre of mining, power generation and the aluminium industry.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/angul-district.jpg" alt="Angul district" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Abhas Kumar Kheti · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Panchadhara_Ghati,_Athmallik.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
